Subject: [PATCH 484/488] Tests: run 24's verification failures; a
 deterministic DSpark stand-in projection

The insertion port's test stood in a seven-argument insertion for the one
rejection_sample now calls with its dead-row cut; the stand-in takes it (None).
The dead-row cap test compared sampled tokens past the uncapped count, which
both paths leave unwritten (new_empty); it compares the written columns. The
capped insertion's declaration test already takes only the early returns
(01b4c3b04).

The DSpark context test projects with an elementwise stand-in instead of a
GEMM, so its reference cannot differ by the GEMM's choice of algorithm.
---
 ...st_deepseek_v41_tilelang_dspark_context.py | 25 +++++++++++--------
 .../test_rejection_sampler_utils.py           | 11 +++++---
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

